# proves the atom map hash aborts with "Concurrent modification of host and device
# hashes" when the map lives on the device.  Special::dedup() runs map_one(), which
# marks the host side dirty, then map_clear(), which marked the device side dirty on
# top of it.  "atom/map device" is the default on a GPU build, so this is the normal
# path there; it must be requested explicitly on a CPU-only build.
#
# run with: -k on t 1 -sf kk -pk kokkos atom/map device
units           lj
atom_style      bond
atom_modify     map hash
boundary        p p p
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box bond/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 14 extra/special/per/atom 200
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 100.0 1.1
create_bonds    many all all 1 1.0 1.25
velocity        all create 1.0 87287 loop geom
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check no
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
run             10
